---
import { RUNS } from "../lib/data";
const r = RUNS[2025];
const wr = r.watchReset!;
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">A note on 2025</p>
    <h2 class="h2">The watch was reset at km <span class="num" style="color: var(--c-2025);">{wr.km}</span>.</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      In 2025, the race began under the wrong workout type on the watch. Around
      the Riflebutts checkpoint at km <span class="num">{wr.km}</span>, it was
      stopped and restarted with the right one — losing roughly one second of
      data between the two files. The site stitches the two halves into a
      single run rather than hide the seam.
    </p>
    <p class="prose muted">
      It's also where the year changes character on the map: the long northbound
      Cape&nbsp;to&nbsp;Cape begins, and the second half of every year has been
      where the bulk of the year‑over‑year improvement has come from.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
